# Orbyt Architecture

Orbyt is a video app for Bluesky built on the AT Protocol. React Native + Expo.

## Project Structure

- `app/` — Expo Router file-based routes (tabs, modals, dynamic routes like `[did]`, `[id]`)
- `src/components/ui/` — Reusable primitives (Icon, Button, Card, Modal, Input, share-sheet)
- `src/components/features/` — Domain modules: feed, video, comments, activity, profile, moderation, badging
- `src/components/layout/` — Headers and navigation (UniversalHeader, ProfileHeader, ChannelHeader, TabNavigation)
- `src/services/` — API layer and business logic (see full breakdown below)
- `src/stores/` — Zustand stores (client state)
- `src/hooks/` — Custom React hooks
- `src/theme/` — Design tokens (`Colors` palette)
- `src/utils/` — Helpers, constants, typography, query config (see full breakdown below)
- `src/context/` — React Context providers (SessionProvider, OverlayLayoutContext, FollowContext, FeedScrollContext)
- `src/core/` — Core modules (visibility system for feed/video playback)

### Services (`src/services/`)

- `api/AtprotoService.tsx` — Main API facade (delegates to sub-services)
- `api/core.ts` — Shared session management and API client setup
- `api/feed/FeedService.ts` — `AtprotoFeedService` class; `app.bsky.feed.*` operations
- `api/graph/GraphService.ts` — `app.bsky.graph.*` operations
- `api/chat/ChatService.ts` — Chat operations
- `api/actor/ActorService.ts` — `app.bsky.actor.*` operations
- `api/notification/NotificationService.ts` — Notification operations
- `api/bookmark/BookmarkService.ts` — Bookmark operations
- `api/video/VideoService.ts` — Video-specific API operations
- `api/repo/RepoService.ts` — `com.atproto.repo.*` operations
- `auth/OAuthService.ts` — OAuth flow
- `auth/EmailVerificationService.ts` — Email verification
- `data/ProfileService.ts` — Profile caching (React Query integration)
- `data/ChannelService.ts` — Channel feed generator caching
- `video/VideoProcessingService.ts` — FFmpeg video processing
- `video/VideoEditingService.ts` — FFmpeg video editing
- `colors/OrbytColors.ts` — Profile color management (fetch, persist, sync)
- `colors/useOrbytColors.tsx` — React hooks for profile colors
- `moderation/ModerationService.ts` — Moderation operations
- `FeedService.ts` — App-level `FeedService` (bookmarks, seen videos); distinct from `AtprotoFeedService`
- `SeenVideoService.ts` — Seen video tracking
- `OrbytBannerService.ts` — Explore header banners (`useHeaders`), featuring popular Communities
- `OrbytChannelsService.ts` — Community directory cache (channels are Orbyt Communities)
- `orbyt/orbytApi.ts` — Orbyt AppView XRPC client (`orbytPublicQuery`, `orbytAuthedCall`)
- `orbyt/communities.ts` — `com.getorbyt.community.*` reads and membership/post-link records
- `orbyt/postCommunities.ts` — batched post → Community lookup (`usePostCommunity`)

### Utilities (`src/utils/`)

- `constants.ts` — `BORDER_RADIUS`, `ANIMATION_CONSTANTS`, `ICON_SIZES`, `QUERY_CONSTANTS`
- `logger.ts` — Centralized logger (never use `console.log`)
- `query/queryKeys.ts` — Centralized React Query key factory
- `query/queryClient.ts` — Query client config with stale times and retry
- `storage/storage.ts` — MMKV instance and Zustand persist adapter
- `formatting/colors.ts` — `hexToRGBA`, `blendColors`, `isColorDark`, `getContrastRatio`, image color extraction
- `formatting/time.ts` — `formatTime` (MM:SS / HH:MM:SS for video durations)
- `formatting/numbers.ts` — `formatNumber` (1.2K, 10K truncation)
- `formatting/handles.ts` — `formatHandle`, `splitHandleSuffix` (AT Protocol handle formatting)
- `video/` — Video path helpers, segment management
- `device/screen.ts` — Screen dimension utilities
- `navigation/` — Tab refs, bottom sheet registry
- `links/bluesky.ts` — Bluesky URL parsing and deep link handling
- `errors/errorHandler.ts` — `ErrorHandler` class, `CommonErrorHandlers`, error type checks
- `errors/oauth.ts` — OAuth-specific error handling
- `channels/orbyt.ts` — Built-in channel definitions and color generation
- `chat/streak.ts` — Chat streak calculations
- `types/richText.ts` — Rich text type definitions
- `components/typography.tsx` — `Typography` tokens, `TypographyText` component
- `components/truesheet/` — `AppTrueSheet`, `trueSheetPresets`, keyboard-aware footer

## State Management

- **Client state**: Zustand stores in `src/stores/` (userStore, appStore, modalStore, uiStore, followStore, etc.)
- **Server state**: TanStack React Query. Query keys in `src/utils/query/queryKeys.ts`, client config in `src/utils/query/queryClient.ts`
- **Persistence**: MMKV via `src/utils/storage/storage.ts`, expo-secure-store for auth credentials

## Provider Hierarchy (app/_layout.tsx)

ThemeProvider → SafeAreaProvider → QueryClientProvider → GestureHandlerRootView → KeyboardProvider → TabBarProvider → OverlayLayoutProvider → SessionProvider → QueryErrorBoundary → RootNavigator

### Splash screen control

Native splash is managed directly in `app/_layout.tsx` via `expo-splash-screen`. The layout holds rendering (returns `null`) until app readiness conditions are met, then calls `SplashScreen.hideAsync()` once to avoid a blank/partial first paint.

## Error Handling

- **ErrorBoundary** (`src/components/ui/ErrorBoundary.tsx`): class component with `level` prop (`root`, `feature`, `component`). Supports `resetKeys`, custom fallback, and error reporting via email.
- **QueryErrorBoundary** (`src/components/ui/QueryErrorBoundary.tsx`): wraps `ErrorBoundary` with `QueryErrorResetBoundary` to reset failed queries on retry. Used at root level in `app/_layout.tsx`.
- **ErrorHandler** (`src/utils/errors/errorHandler.ts`): centralized error utility with `handleError`, `safeAsync`, `safeSync`, and type checks (`isNetworkError`, `isAuthError`, `isUserCancellation`).
- **CommonErrorHandlers**: predefined handlers for login, logout, feed load, video playback, navigation, cache, and API errors.
- Log all errors through `logger` with context. Use `ErrorHandler.safeAsync()` for fire-and-forget operations.

## Conventions

- **Path aliases**: `@/*` → `src/*`, `@stores/*` → `src/stores/*`
- **Naming**: Components = PascalCase, hooks = `use*`, stores = `*Store`, services = `*Service`
- **Directories**: Multi-word directory names use kebab-case (e.g. `share-sheet`, `hidden-posts`)
- **Files**: Filename matches primary export (e.g. `VideoCard.tsx` exports `VideoCard`)
- **New components**: UI primitives → `components/ui/`, feature code → `components/features/<domain>/`, layout → `components/layout/`
- **Barrel exports**: Check existing barrels before adding exports: `src/components/index.ts`, `src/hooks/index.ts`, `src/services/index.ts`, `src/stores/index.ts`
- **Logging**: Use `logger` from `src/utils/logger` — never `console.log`
- **TypeScript**: Avoid `any`; use proper types or `unknown`
- **Functional components**: Always prefer functional components with hooks. Class components only for error boundaries (React limitation).
- **Dependencies first**: Before writing custom utility functions, check if an installed dependency or `src/utils/` module already provides the functionality. Prefer battle-tested library functions over custom implementations (e.g. `date-fns` for date operations, `Intl` APIs for formatting, Expo SDK modules over third-party alternatives). Check the Utilities section above before creating new helpers.
- **Existing utilities**: Before building new helpers, check `src/utils/formatting/` (colors, time, numbers, handles), `src/utils/errors/` (ErrorHandler), `src/utils/video/`, `src/utils/links/`, `src/utils/device/`, and `src/utils/navigation/`.
